The losses of the war are not recorded in any form, and the figure generally adopted for the mortality of the campaign is of the order of 90 per cent of the population of the annexed lands, killed or enslaved. That gives some 43,900 people lost to the two peoples, and a surviving population of the order of 4,900, of whom part were absorbed into the labouring population of the colony and part withdrew into the territories of neighbouring peoples.

The 43,900 are divided in the modern literature between those who died and those who were taken captive. Death is estimated to have accounted for the greater part, on the evidence of the disease that accompanied the campaign and of the settlements found abandoned or containing the unburied dead. The estimate generally given is of the order of 32,500 dead and some 11,400 taken captive and sold into the plantation economy of the colony.

The captive population of about 11,400 was, for this period, the whole of the colony's enslaved population. The [[Secret Trade]], which in the following century carried enslaved people from [[Dagit]] and the [[Balausia Peninsula]] to the Sinchew plantations, had not begun, and the labour of the colony was supplied until the 1560s by the captives of the western war and by indentured settlers from Zong.

== Territorial change ==

[[File:Sinchew 1558.png|thumb|center|700px|The territory of the [[Sinchew Colony]] in 1558, after the annexation of the Salowi and Chidoha lands. The colony's territory before the war is shown in red; the territory added by the war is shown in green.]]
<!-- Image prompt: two-panel before-and-after locator map of Sinchew, 1549 and 1558, within the outline of the modern country; original colony in red, annexed western lands in green, Kawesa territories cream, other peoples grey, ocean light blue, no legend -->

The colony's territory at the outbreak of the war was about 164,582 km², comprising the lands north of the [[Hachinawa|Hahkina]] frontier and the coast around [[Tamsui]]. The lands annexed from the Salowi and Chidoha added about 203,192 km², the two territories being almost wholly outside the colony's existing boundaries. The colony's extent after the war was about 367,764 km², an increase of some 124 per cent on its previous size.

== Aftermath ==

The Salowi and the Chidoha were defeated and their lands annexed to the Sinchew Colony. The peoples were killed, displaced or enslaved; survivors were absorbed into the labouring population of the colony or withdrew into the territory of other peoples.

The annexation supplied the colony with the land its settlers and plantations required. The campaign had been fought with forces belonging to no government and against peoples whom the law of the crown nominally protected.

